{{High Risk|Template:Track|nocat=1|pagetype=Main}}
Renders a single '''track row''' for an album or discography tracklist.

'''Important:''' this template outputs a raw <code><nowiki><tr></nowiki></code> row, so it '''must''' be placed inside HTML <code><nowiki><table>…</table></nowiki></code> tags — not inside a wikitable (<code><nowiki>{|</nowiki></code>) — and the table needs its own header row. Each call produces seven cells, or eight when <code>group</code> is used, so the header row must have a matching number of columns. This template works inside {{T|AlbumType2}}

==Syntax==
{{T|Track|block=1
|v1=number
|v2=title =
|v3=additionalshortinfo =
|v4=singers =
|v5=lyricist =
|v6=composer =
|v7=arranger =
|v8=group =
}}

==Examples==
<pre>
<table class="wikitable">
<tr><th>#</th><th>Title</th><th>Info</th><th>Singers</th><th>Lyricist</th><th>Composer</th><th>Arranger</th></tr>
{{Track|1|title=Song Title 1|additionalshortinfo=Single|singers=Artist A|lyricist=Writer A|composer=Composer A|arranger=Arranger A}}
{{Track|2|title=Song Title 2|additionalshortinfo=Instrumental|singers=Artist B|lyricist=Writer B|composer=Composer B|arranger=Arranger B}}
</table>
</pre>

